  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Saturday)\nIssued at 910 AM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nMean western NOAM ridging will support mild and dry weather \nthrough most of the period as Pac flow continues aloft. \nWeak/skirting impulses will support cool fronts at times to knock \ntemps down a few degrees and support passing breezy days. Temps \nwill be above normal in the period most days. Upper trough \ntraversing southern Canada today with warm SW downslope flow ahead\nof this system. Breezy SW winds can be expected with a few gusts \nover 40 mph possible in northeast WY. Cool front will move through\nearly Monday with winds shifting NW. Expect cooler but still \nabove normal highs Monday with highs in the 50s and 60s. The next \nsystem will move into the region Tues with warmer temps expected. \nIt looks potentially breezy Tues behind the expected sfc trough in\nthe afternoon. A stronger back door cool front may slide into the\nregion later Wed, which could knock down temps substantially \nacross the SD Plains Thur. Models are offering varying solutions \nper local heights, indicating lower confidence in how far west \nthis system will impact temps. However, any cool down will be \nshort lived as the western NOAM ridge quickly rebuilds into the \nregion, supporting a very mild and dry next weekend.",
